{"body":"**`active` is false for a configured-but-open OIDC deployment, and the UI then says the mode is not configured.** `_named_gates` only adds the OIDC gate when `generic_oidc_configured AND oidc_allowlist_configured`. With `OIDC_ISSUER`/`OIDC_AUDIENCE` set and no allowlist (the `auth_oidc_no_signup_allowlist` WARNING state), both OIDC rows come back `active=false` and `WorkspaceConfigPanels.tsx:51` renders "Not read — sign-in mode not configured". The mode *is* configured; the truth is "no app-side allowlist: every identity the issuer vouches for is admitted", which is exactly the posture an admin opening this card needs to see (#1386 class). Azure AD mode has the same shape: all four rows read "mode not configured" and nothing says the tenant is the gate. Derive `active` from the mode (`generic_oidc_configured` / `otp_auth_configured`) and add an explicit `open: bool` (or a third status) for "mode configured, list empty".

