{"body":"**`WORKSPACE_ADMIN_EMAILS` does admit sign-in, so the `grants` split and the guide are false.** `env_verdict` returns `GRANTED` when `s.is_admin_email(email)`, and `_decide` admits on `GRANTED` with no member row even under enforcement (`membership_service.py:150-163, 193-200`). The field comment ("`sign_in` admits the address; `admin_role` grants Admin") implies this row does *not* admit, and `docs/site/guides/admin.md:405` states it outright: "which never admits anyone by itself". An admin removing a leaver from Members while they remain in this variable will believe the account is gone; it is not, and it signs in as Admin. State the row as "admits and grants Admin" (e.g. `grants: "sign_in_and_admin_role"`) and fix the guide line.

