Notes on what was checked and found clean: `SessionLocal` has `autoflush=False`, so `set_tags`' lazy loads/inserts cannot flush the check's dirty state ahead of the `is_modified` version gate; `update_connection` reads `versioned_change` before `set_tags` and audits on every update; `expire_on_commit` reloads tags in sorted order for the response; FK cascades + `passive_deletes` are consistent between model and migration; the `useAsyncData` `setTagFilter(); reload()` pattern on Suites is correct because both updates batch into one render. The two findings that matter most are the Alembic double-head (will break the migrate job on merge) and the SuiteForm field placement (silently deletes tags on non-sampling datasources).

